      "content": "Absolutely, let's add that level of detail:\n\n1. The \"Old Money\" / Heritage Segment: We want to evoke a sense of classic respectability, so we'll consider a demographic with more mature skin tones, polished features, and sophisticated attire. Think salt-and-pepper hair, well-groomed but not overly trendy hairstyles, and complexions that mature gracefully. Their fashion preferences lean towards timeless pieces like tweed jackets, tailored suits, and crisp white shirts. Their look should convey an air of understated wealth, leaning on natural, understated – and subtle – high-end materials and patterns, such as monogrammed leather goods, heathered silks, or muted plaid.\n\n2. The \"Urban Trendy\" / Mass-Market Segment: This segment is all about visual impact, so we should channel their energy into vibrant skin tones, busy textures, and daring styles that reflect modern, urban life. They prefer bolder fashion choices like graphic tees, cropped hoodies with eye-catching prints, and oversized sneakers with big-city flair. Think about pairing these items with statement accessories, such as chunky jewelry and bright sneakers. This group craves \"fast fashion,\" therefore items that capture this vibe should emphasize affordable pieces from trendy brands, perhaps in unconventional",
